WEBVTT

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:13.950
Man, yesterday was a surprise!

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:16.950
To think you're doing your
homestay at my house.

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:19.660
From now on, we'll be
eating from the same pot!

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:22.200
Where'd you pick up that expression?

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:24.870
Your Japanese really is good.

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:26.160
How'd you learn it?

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:28.330
I studied it by watching anime.

00:00:28.330 --> 00:00:31.080
Oh, it really seems like that!

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:35.450
Well, whatever. If you ever have trouble
with the culture gap, I'm happy to help.

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:36.870
Thank you.

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:38.700
But it's no problem!

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:43.080
Watching Jackie Chan movies really
helped me understand Japanese culture!

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:45.450
So your study method was
flawed from the start.

00:02:15.950 --> 00:02:20.950
"Episode 7
'Want to Be an Idol?'"

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:22.370
What did you say?!

00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:24.450
The gym's closed today?!

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:26.830
Yup, every third Monday of the month.

00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:28.700
Oh... Oh, no...

00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:31.700
It's so boring when the gym's closed.

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:33.080
<i>Blyad</i>!

00:02:33.080 --> 00:02:36.500
My revenge will have to wait another day!

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:38.950
You're still serious about that?

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:42.330
I know! Why don't we have
a welcome party for you today?

00:02:42.330 --> 00:02:46.000
Huh? Really? In that case,
I'd like to visit Hong Kong.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:47.250
Is it close to our school?

00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:49.250
That's not even part of Japan!

00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:50.200
Oh!

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:53.330
Sorry, I have work today.

00:02:53.330 --> 00:02:56.080
Wait, why don't you all
come eat at my place?

00:02:56.540 --> 00:02:59.540
"Charcoal-Grilled Yakiniku Sakura"

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:02.660
All right! Here's some first-class <i>galbi</i>!

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:06.120
It smells so good!

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:07.410
Looks delicious!

00:03:07.410 --> 00:03:09.370
It should be pretty much done.

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:10.660
Well, then...

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:12.870
Let's dig in!

00:03:17.410 --> 00:03:18.250
Delish!

00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:20.580
This is my first time eating Japanese BBQ!

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:23.120
So your family runs a <i>yakiniku </i>restaurant?

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:25.250
No, no.

00:03:25.250 --> 00:03:28.080
My older brother opened this place
after ditching the salaryman life.

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:31.500
I help out when we're a few hands short.

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:33.500
Wow, so that's why...

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:35.200
What a sad story...

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:37.450
Yeah, totally...

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:40.330
You guys have got meat on the brain.

00:03:40.330 --> 00:03:42.000
My friends, rejoice!

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:44.370
Today, you get a special friendship discount!

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:46.660
In return, you can advertise the place!

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:48.000
--Thanks!
--Thank you!
--<i>Spasiba </i>[Thank you]!

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:51.660
Now I get it.

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:54.000
This is the secret of Hibiki's strength.

00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:59.580
She needs nutrients to build muscles...

00:03:59.580 --> 00:04:05.620
...one of which is protein,
and the king of all animal protein is...

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:07.000
...beef!

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:08.500
"*Gina's personal opinion"

00:04:08.500 --> 00:04:13.160
--All right, eat up!
--A <i>yakiniku </i>restaurant is the perfect
environment to take in protein.

00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:16.620
And if she gets paid to work here,
it's two birds with one stone.

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:18.450
Right, I'll keep bringing you more.

00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:20.120
Great!

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:23.950
On that note, we'll talk about beef today!

00:04:23.950 --> 00:04:27.160
Everybody loves high-calorie,
high-protein beef!

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:30.830
An essential part of a bodybuilding diet!

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:32.790
Okay, here's some tenderloin!

00:04:32.790 --> 00:04:34.250
But wait!

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:38.620
Cuts from different parts of the cow
vary greatly in nutritional value.

00:04:38.870 --> 00:04:40.620
"Tenderloin"
"Roughly 220 kcal/100 g"

00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:42.580
"Tenderloin"
"Roughly 220 kcal/100 g"
Take tenderloin, for example!

00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:45.620
This is a low-calorie cut rich in protein.

00:04:46.750 --> 00:04:48.870
Here's some liver!

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:50.660
"Liver"
"Roughly 130 kcal/100 g"

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:52.540
"Liver"
"Roughly 130 kcal/100 g"
Liver is low-calorie!

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:54.750
Eating it also helps prevent anemia!

00:04:55.950 --> 00:04:58.450
Here's some <i>galbi</i>!

00:04:58.540 --> 00:05:00.250
"<i>Galbi</i>"
"Roughly 520 kcal/100 g"

00:05:00.250 --> 00:05:02.160
"<i>Galbi</i>"
"Roughly 520 kcal/100 g"
<i>Galbi </i>is nutrient rich

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:04.370
"<i>Galbi</i>"
"Roughly 520 kcal/100 g"
but high in sugar and calories,

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:05.830
so make sure not to eat too much!

00:05:06.790 --> 00:05:13.040
"Imported Sirloin"  "Calories"  "Japanese Sirloin"
"Roughly 300 kcal"                  "Roughly 500 kcal"
What's more, Japanese cuts tend to
have more calories than imported beef.

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:18.870
If you want to diet, you can lower your
calorie intake with imported cuts.

00:05:18.870 --> 00:05:22.080
Mm! This is simply delicious!

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:24.620
<i>Harasho</i>! <i>Spasiba</i>! <i>Tovarish </i>[Comrade]!

00:05:24.620 --> 00:05:26.790
Gina, you've switched to Russian.

00:05:26.790 --> 00:05:28.620
But it really is good.

00:05:28.620 --> 00:05:30.080
Hey, that <i>galbi</i>'s mine!

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:32.330
--I've been getting it ready to eat!
--And nobody's listening...

00:05:32.330 --> 00:05:34.700
--I've been getting it ready to eat!
--Young people have fearsome appetites.

00:05:36.450 --> 00:05:39.660
You can't get a good body
through training alone!

00:05:39.660 --> 00:05:42.200
Make sure you watch what you eat, too!

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:44.870
The people left out of this segment
muscled their way in at the end!

00:05:45.750 --> 00:05:48.160
Oh, it's already late.

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:51.540
I'll grab some food while it's quiet.

00:05:51.540 --> 00:05:54.120
Looks like Hibiki's going to eat now.

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:57.330
I'm curious to know what
food fuels her superpowers.

00:05:57.330 --> 00:05:59.580
I'll secretly observe her.

00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:04.830
Time to eat!

00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:06.410
Huh?

00:06:06.410 --> 00:06:07.410
"Beef Roast" "Rice (6 Helpings)"
"Two Fried & Salted Mackerel" "Meat Sauce Spaghetti"
What?

00:06:07.410 --> 00:06:08.910
"Beef Roast" "Rice (6 Helpings)"
"Two Fried & Salted Mackerel" "Meat Sauce Spaghetti"
Before I consider her meat intake,

00:06:08.910 --> 00:06:10.200
"Beef Roast" "Rice (6 Helpings)"
"Two Fried & Salted Mackerel" "Meat Sauce Spaghetti"
what's up with these serving sizes?!

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:12.120
"Beef Roast" "Rice (6 Helpings)"
"Two Fried & Salted Mackerel" "Meat Sauce Spaghetti"
What the hell? Is that one meal's worth?!

00:06:13.700 --> 00:06:17.080
W-Wait, I've heard of something like this...

00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:19.620
It was about a Japanese pro wrestler.

00:06:19.620 --> 00:06:25.950
Back when he started out, the hardest
thing wasn't the training or the injuries...

00:06:25.950 --> 00:06:28.200
It was eating.

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:32.830
Every day, he trained like mad
from dawn to dusk.

00:06:32.830 --> 00:06:36.250
He only took a break for meals,
and despite feeling sick from exhaustion,

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:41.370
he was forced to eat beyond
his limit to build up his body.

00:06:41.370 --> 00:06:47.370
When he couldn't eat anymore, he'd blend it
all up and make himself to drink it.

00:06:47.370 --> 00:06:49.040
--Mm, delicious!

00:06:49.040 --> 00:06:52.040
--So a diet that makes tough pro wrestlers cringe
--Mm, delicious!

00:06:52.040 --> 00:06:53.450
--So a diet that makes tough pro wrestlers cringe
--This is the best!

00:06:53.450 --> 00:06:57.080
--is the secret behind her strength...
--This is the best!

00:06:57.080 --> 00:06:58.790
I could eat this until the day I die!

00:07:01.830 --> 00:07:07.120
Of course, seeing you work hard
every day to become ever stronger...

00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:10.540
...makes me want to defeat
you even more, Hibiki!

00:07:10.540 --> 00:07:13.450
Aren't you eating too much again?

00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:16.410
Today's my cheat day, so it's fine.

00:07:16.410 --> 00:07:18.660
She just enjoys eating.

00:07:19.450 --> 00:07:21.410
Phew, I ate the whole thing!

00:07:21.410 --> 00:07:24.160
Well then, back to work.

00:07:24.160 --> 00:07:25.830
You work five days a week?

00:07:25.830 --> 00:07:27.160
Must be hard!

00:07:27.160 --> 00:07:29.540
Well, it sure isn't easy.

00:07:29.540 --> 00:07:32.750
I wish I could at least take gym days off.

00:07:32.750 --> 00:07:36.410
I mean, Silverman Gym's monthly
fees are pretty expensive.

00:07:36.410 --> 00:07:39.580
And my food expenses are stupidly high.

00:07:39.580 --> 00:07:42.750
I won't have enough money
if I don't work this much.

00:07:44.330 --> 00:07:47.200
Hibiki, do you really not know?

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:48.290
Know what?

00:07:48.290 --> 00:07:55.120
You can ask our school to cover your gym
fees and all training-related expenses.

00:07:55.910 --> 00:07:57.200
You can what?!

00:07:57.200 --> 00:08:00.160
My sister's chairman of the board,
and her motto is,

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:04.370
"Students should learn things outside of
school, especially strength training."

00:08:04.370 --> 00:08:07.200
She's serious about funding
her own personal hobby!

00:08:07.200 --> 00:08:12.000
That means my sister will personally grant
you money to pay for your training fees.

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:16.290
Just how rich is our chair--
I mean, your family?!

00:08:16.290 --> 00:08:18.200
But still, that means...

00:08:18.200 --> 00:08:19.910
That means...

00:08:19.910 --> 00:08:21.830
Yay!

00:08:21.830 --> 00:08:24.910
I need to ask them to cover the
membership fees I've paid for right away!

00:08:24.910 --> 00:08:29.370
--Of course, you'll still pay for your food.
--Yes! That's it! Yay!

00:08:29.950 --> 00:08:31.080
"Charcoal-Grilled Yakiniku Sakura"

00:08:31.080 --> 00:08:34.950
"Charcoal-Grilled Yakiniku Sakura"
Thus, Hibiki's money woes came to an end.

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:41.370
"Micronesia"        "South Pacific" "Oceania"
"Melanesia"   "Polynesia"
"Australia" "New Zealand"
Okay, please open your textbooks.

00:08:41.370 --> 00:08:45.540
Today, we'll study the cultures of Oceania.

00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:48.700
--So this teacher goes to the same gym
as Hibiki and the others...
--Oceania refers to the South Pacific area.

00:08:48.700 --> 00:08:49.910
--So this teacher goes to the same gym
as Hibiki and the others...
--You've heard of Australia and New Zealand,

00:08:49.910 --> 00:08:51.750
--I think she's Satomi Tachibana-<i>sensei</i>...
--You've heard of Australia and New Zealand,

00:08:51.750 --> 00:08:53.950
--I think she's Satomi Tachibana-<i>sensei</i>...
--but it also includes Polynesia, Melanesia,

00:08:53.950 --> 00:08:54.790
--Huh?
--but it also includes Polynesia, Melanesia,

00:08:54.790 --> 00:08:56.290
--Huh?
--and Micronesia, as well as countless small islands.

00:08:56.290 --> 00:08:58.330
--Where have I seen that mole before?
--and Micronesia, as well as countless small islands.

00:08:58.330 --> 00:09:00.330
--Where have I seen that mole before?
--Before European contact,

00:09:00.330 --> 00:09:01.000
--they had already developed

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:02.950
--What?
--they had already developed

00:09:02.950 --> 00:09:04.080
--a uniquely impressive civilization and culture.

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:06.330
--No, no, it couldn't be...
--a uniquely impressive civilization and culture.

00:09:09.450 --> 00:09:13.120
Then let's have someone read this page for us.

00:09:13.120 --> 00:09:15.580
How about the person
whose student number is 12?

00:09:16.660 --> 00:09:17.910
I'm sure of it!

00:09:17.910 --> 00:09:18.910
She's...

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:21.700
...Yulia Riko!

00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:23.910
Satomi's in big trouble!

00:09:25.200 --> 00:09:26.330
Hello, everyone!

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:29.540
Today, let's work hard to train our...

00:09:29.540 --> 00:09:30.830
...muscles!

00:09:30.830 --> 00:09:33.910
What's this? Are Tachibana-<i>sensei</i>
and Gina taking a day off?

00:09:33.910 --> 00:09:37.660
Apparently, Sensei had some important
business to deal with and couldn't come.

00:09:37.660 --> 00:09:38.870
--Gina went somewhere early this morning.

00:09:38.870 --> 00:09:40.660
--<i>Da svidanya</i>!
--Gina went somewhere early this morning.

00:09:40.660 --> 00:09:42.950
Said she had something important to do.

00:09:42.950 --> 00:09:46.160
Maybe they're doing something together?

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:48.330
Yeah, right, it's just a coincidence.

00:09:48.330 --> 00:09:51.080
"Photo Studio
Studio SM"
Those two probably have nothing in common.

00:09:57.080 --> 00:10:00.290
Great! That's great! Super <i>harasho</i>!

00:10:00.290 --> 00:10:03.790
Put on a more somber expression,
<i>pozhaluysta </i>[please]!

00:10:03.790 --> 00:10:05.830
This is painful.

00:10:05.830 --> 00:10:08.040
What a beautiful sight!

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:11.950
Meeting the real Yulia Riko makes me
<i>spasiba </i>from the bottom of my heart!

00:10:11.950 --> 00:10:14.790
Gina-<i>san</i>, please keep your voice down!

00:10:14.790 --> 00:10:17.540
Augh, how did it come to this...?

00:10:18.700 --> 00:10:20.580
Tachibana-<i>sensei</i>.

00:10:20.580 --> 00:10:22.500
I know who you really are.

00:10:22.500 --> 00:10:25.200
Huh? Wh-What? What are you talking about?

00:10:25.200 --> 00:10:27.250
Don't play dumb.

00:10:27.250 --> 00:10:31.000
This mole under her eye
exactly matches yours.

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:35.580
Tachibana-<i>sensei</i>, you're the
famous cosplayer Yulia Riko, right?

00:10:37.950 --> 00:10:40.750
This is bad! This is really bad!

00:10:40.750 --> 00:10:43.250
If my borderline pornographic
cosplay hobby comes to light,

00:10:43.250 --> 00:10:45.500
then my position as a teacher is toast!

00:10:45.500 --> 00:10:47.700
This is a disaster!

00:10:48.870 --> 00:10:51.700
Please, keep this a secret!

00:10:51.700 --> 00:10:54.160
I'll be your slave for life!

00:10:54.160 --> 00:10:56.750
Uh, I don't plan on telling anyone...

00:10:56.750 --> 00:10:58.830
And what's with that offer?

00:10:58.830 --> 00:11:02.120
I love anime and cosplayers.

00:11:02.120 --> 00:11:04.410
I don't want to destroy your reputation.

00:11:04.410 --> 00:11:06.450
I can't believe you'd be so altruistic!

00:11:06.450 --> 00:11:09.660
I'm begging you, tell me your terms!

00:11:09.660 --> 00:11:13.540
What kind of life have you led
to have such a warped way of thinking?!

00:11:13.540 --> 00:11:16.120
Okay, then, if that's what you want...

00:11:16.830 --> 00:11:23.000
And that's why she's spending the whole
day hanging out with Tachibana-<i>sensei</i>.

00:11:23.000 --> 00:11:25.500
So let's go to Akihabara next!

00:11:25.500 --> 00:11:27.410
And I'd like to go to Macao tonight!

00:11:27.410 --> 00:11:29.290
I don't think we could...

00:11:29.290 --> 00:11:30.870
That's not Japan.

00:11:32.910 --> 00:11:34.540
Ow, ow, ow, ow...

00:11:34.540 --> 00:11:36.540
What's wrong, Sensei?

00:11:36.540 --> 00:11:39.870
Oh, I'm fine. I'm just a bit sore.

00:11:39.870 --> 00:11:42.160
I really overdid it at the gym recently.

00:11:42.160 --> 00:11:46.410
I still hurt all over three days later.

00:11:46.410 --> 00:11:49.950
My, my, it takes a lot longer
to heal up when you get older.

00:11:49.950 --> 00:11:51.250
Huh...

00:11:51.250 --> 00:11:53.660
Sensei, is Akihabara far from here?

00:11:53.660 --> 00:11:57.950
"Suidobashi"    "Close"    "Akihabara"
Not really. You'll get there in a flash
by train, but you can also walk there.

00:11:57.950 --> 00:12:00.410
"Suidobashi"    "Close"    "Akihabara"
I see! Then this is perfect!

00:12:00.410 --> 00:12:04.660
Let's skip the train and recover
our strength by jogging instead!

00:12:04.660 --> 00:12:06.620
That's called active rest!

00:12:06.620 --> 00:12:10.000
Huh? You can relieve fatigue with jogging?

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:12.200
Wouldn't running tire you out?

00:12:12.200 --> 00:12:17.700
Do you happen to take a long rest to
recover in the days after your workout?

00:12:17.700 --> 00:12:18.870
Like this.

00:12:18.870 --> 00:12:22.290
It's true that I relax more than usual.

00:12:22.290 --> 00:12:25.160
I'll ignore how offensive
this image feels for now.

00:12:25.160 --> 00:12:30.620
But if you just laze around,
it actually takes you longer to recharge.

00:12:30.620 --> 00:12:32.120
What did you say?!

00:12:32.120 --> 00:12:33.700
Improving your blood circulation
is an important part of reducing fatigue.

00:12:33.700 --> 00:12:36.910
"Oxygen"
Improving your blood circulation
is an important part of reducing fatigue.

00:12:36.910 --> 00:12:39.580
"Oxygen"
It spreads oxygen throughout your body.

00:12:39.580 --> 00:12:43.540
Light exercise helps
improve blood circulation.

00:12:43.540 --> 00:12:46.040
That's what I mean by active rest.

00:12:46.040 --> 00:12:48.200
Essentially, you stimulate recovery.

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:51.160
I get it now. So that's why
you mentioned jogging.

00:12:51.160 --> 00:12:53.500
It doesn't have to be jogging.

00:12:53.500 --> 00:12:58.580
Walking, swimming, stretching,
and light weight training all work.

00:12:58.580 --> 00:13:02.450
If you're going to do active rest,
there's two things to consider.

00:13:02.450 --> 00:13:04.620
First of all...

00:13:04.620 --> 00:13:07.450
...don't go full throttle and increase
the intensity of your workout too much.

00:13:08.290 --> 00:13:10.500
At that point it's no longer "rest."

00:13:13.370 --> 00:13:20.370
And second of all, if you're sick or hurt,
you should heal up with passive rest.

00:13:20.370 --> 00:13:22.120
Don't push yourself too much.

00:13:22.120 --> 00:13:23.700
That's how it works.

00:13:23.700 --> 00:13:26.450
So let's jog to Akihabara!

00:13:26.450 --> 00:13:27.660
Got it!

00:13:42.580 --> 00:13:44.950
Active rest and passive rest!

00:13:44.950 --> 00:13:47.910
Do both based on how you feel!

00:13:47.910 --> 00:13:49.700
Machio-<i>san</i>, what's gotten into you?!

00:13:50.450 --> 00:13:53.450
Huh, so this is what active rest is like.

00:13:53.450 --> 00:13:56.620
Make sure not to bounce too much.

00:13:56.620 --> 00:13:59.250
Will it have an impact at this speed?

00:13:59.250 --> 00:14:01.830
It feels no different from walking.

00:14:01.830 --> 00:14:05.290
Of course! Actually, slower is better.

00:14:05.290 --> 00:14:07.660
Our goal is to feel refreshed, after all.

00:14:07.660 --> 00:14:12.790
As a rough speed guideline, a good pace is
one where you can carry on a conversation.

00:14:12.790 --> 00:14:14.500
I see!

00:14:14.500 --> 00:14:18.540
By the way, why do you
want to go to Akihabara?

00:14:18.540 --> 00:14:20.290
Are you going to buy some electronics?

00:14:22.200 --> 00:14:24.410
Isn't it obvious?

00:14:24.410 --> 00:14:26.290
Akihabara means...

00:14:27.120 --> 00:14:28.330
...idols!

00:14:28.330 --> 00:14:30.410
"Idols"
Idols...?

00:14:30.410 --> 00:14:34.410
After discovering anime, I got addicted
to cosplayers, bonsai, kung-fu movies,

00:14:34.410 --> 00:14:37.160
Japanese food, <i>manzai</i>, yoga, and so on...

00:14:37.160 --> 00:14:40.080
I fell in love with everything
about Japanese culture!

00:14:40.080 --> 00:14:42.910
You've got some non-Japanese
things mixed in there...

00:14:42.910 --> 00:14:47.250
And what I'm most into now is idols!

00:14:47.250 --> 00:14:49.330
Idols, of all things...

00:14:49.330 --> 00:14:51.870
There's a surprisingly large
number of female fans, too.

00:14:51.870 --> 00:14:55.370
An idol I like is doing
an in-store show today.

00:14:55.370 --> 00:14:57.830
I really want to see it live...

00:14:57.830 --> 00:15:00.080
...as her future rival.

00:15:00.080 --> 00:15:01.750
Rival?

00:15:01.750 --> 00:15:03.290
Sensei...

00:15:03.290 --> 00:15:08.040
I came to study in Japan
for a very specific reason.

00:15:08.040 --> 00:15:10.950
I'm no longer satisfied with
just watching them.

00:15:10.950 --> 00:15:13.500
I want to become one myself!

00:15:13.500 --> 00:15:18.620
I'm going to create the strongest
idol unit that ever existed!

00:15:18.620 --> 00:15:21.120
Why are you including me as a member?!

00:15:21.120 --> 00:15:22.540
W-Wait just a minute!

00:15:22.540 --> 00:15:25.580
A teacher becoming an idol is
understandably a very bad idea!

00:15:25.580 --> 00:15:27.660
"*Totally thinks they can pull it off"
Don't worry, we'll figure something out!

00:15:27.660 --> 00:15:29.250
No, we won't!

00:15:29.250 --> 00:15:33.910
Actually, I thought that we could all
participate in an audition next week.

00:15:33.910 --> 00:15:35.580
This plot twist is way too abrupt!

00:15:35.580 --> 00:15:38.410
And besides, the others don't
know anything about this!

00:15:39.290 --> 00:15:41.910
You're suspicious of altruism, right?

00:15:41.910 --> 00:15:45.120
So you're gonna help me, Yulia Riko!

00:15:47.160 --> 00:15:49.410
--Good, good! Keep it up!
--I see...

00:15:49.410 --> 00:15:51.330
--Good, good! Keep it up!
--Seems like things are getting interesting.

00:15:55.410 --> 00:15:57.910
"So Cool!
Public Idol Audition"
"Aspire to Be a Real Idol!"

00:15:57.910 --> 00:16:00.910
"Public Idol Audition"

00:16:00.910 --> 00:16:02.080
"Director Kutaro Deire"

00:16:02.080 --> 00:16:04.790
"Director Kutaro Deire"
Another lackluster audition.

00:16:04.790 --> 00:16:06.660
Director of the So Cool! Idol Audition:

00:16:06.660 --> 00:16:10.290
"Kutaro Deire"
Kutaro Deire.

00:16:10.290 --> 00:16:15.540
Normal girls of a normal level of cuteness
that can sing and dance normally

00:16:15.540 --> 00:16:18.540
and will likely achieve normal popularity.

00:16:18.540 --> 00:16:20.910
They're a dime a dozen these days...

00:16:20.910 --> 00:16:23.160
I don't need girls like that.

00:16:23.160 --> 00:16:24.910
Idols shouldn't be "normal."

00:16:24.910 --> 00:16:26.790
Next, please.

00:16:27.450 --> 00:16:32.080
Idols aren't like that. I wanna see
something more unconventional.

00:16:33.580 --> 00:16:35.290
That's a tall order.

00:16:35.290 --> 00:16:38.040
That kind of talent is beyond rare.

00:16:38.040 --> 00:16:39.450
Yes, thank you.

00:16:39.450 --> 00:16:41.620
Let's have the next group, please.

00:16:45.000 --> 00:16:47.790
Hi, everybody!

00:16:47.790 --> 00:16:50.330
These girls are way too unconventional!

00:16:50.330 --> 00:16:54.410
We're a group of friends who
work out at Silverman Gym.

00:16:54.410 --> 00:16:58.950
And the assistants who came in with us
are also all members of the gym.

00:16:59.580 --> 00:17:00.450
"Everyone From Silverman Gym"

00:17:00.450 --> 00:17:04.160
"Everyone From Silverman Gym"
We don't know them too well,
but they happily agreed to help us.

00:17:04.160 --> 00:17:06.620
"Everyone From Silverman Gym"
At least ask some macho dudes you know!

00:17:06.620 --> 00:17:08.040
We are...

00:17:08.040 --> 00:17:09.790
...the Muscle Gals!

00:17:09.790 --> 00:17:11.410
We're determined to become idols!

00:17:11.410 --> 00:17:12.950
That name will never work!

00:17:12.950 --> 00:17:14.750
Stop it with these poor decisions!

00:17:16.830 --> 00:17:17.870
Aw, jeez...

00:17:17.870 --> 00:17:19.950
I'd written off this lukewarm audition...

00:17:19.950 --> 00:17:22.290
...and then got hit with this
unexpected bombshell!

00:17:22.580 --> 00:17:25.080
"Public Idol Audition"

00:17:25.370 --> 00:17:30.330
Could these girls be the
talent that I'm looking for?

00:17:33.200 --> 00:17:37.910
E-Excuse me. Before you show us your
specialties, I'd like to ask a question.

00:17:37.910 --> 00:17:42.870
Why is just one of you
wearing a kendo mask?

00:17:42.870 --> 00:17:46.000
Hello. My current name is "F*ck the Budo."

00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:48.160
I'm not cool with showing my face.

00:17:48.160 --> 00:17:50.870
Quit it with these names already!

00:17:50.870 --> 00:17:53.620
Why would someone who doesn't want
to show their face want to be an idol?!

00:17:53.620 --> 00:17:56.290
I'm not doing this because I want to!

00:17:56.290 --> 00:17:59.160
I really thought everyone would say no...

00:17:59.160 --> 00:18:00.700
Idols?! Let's do it!

00:18:00.700 --> 00:18:01.700
Sounds fun!

00:18:01.700 --> 00:18:03.500
It'll be a good experience!

00:18:03.500 --> 00:18:06.830
You're all on board with this?!

00:18:06.830 --> 00:18:08.160
Oh, well.

00:18:08.160 --> 00:18:12.870
I'll have done my duty with this. Now I just
need to stay quiet and inconspicuous.

00:18:14.410 --> 00:18:16.410
I-I won't back down!

00:18:16.410 --> 00:18:18.160
I won't crack under pressure!

00:18:18.160 --> 00:18:20.540
O-Okay, then.

00:18:20.540 --> 00:18:23.790
Please take turns showing us your specialties.

00:18:23.790 --> 00:18:27.700
We both do hand-to-hand combat,
so we're going to spar!

00:18:27.700 --> 00:18:30.330
We're going to do some bench presses!

00:18:30.330 --> 00:18:33.950
Are you really trying to be idols?!

00:18:33.950 --> 00:18:36.250
Well, no big deal.

00:18:36.250 --> 00:18:39.120
After all, this is just a ruse
to give them some character, right?

00:18:39.120 --> 00:18:42.660
There are girls who do outlandish
stunts to stand out from the crowd...

00:18:45.660 --> 00:18:49.410
More! You can do more, Hibiki!

00:18:49.410 --> 00:18:51.290
This is some high-level stuff!

00:18:51.620 --> 00:18:54.120
"Public Idol Audition"

00:18:54.250 --> 00:18:56.750
Right, that's how you do it!

00:18:56.750 --> 00:18:58.450
I got a nosebleed...

00:18:58.450 --> 00:18:59.870
Nice bulk, Hibiki!

00:19:01.080 --> 00:19:05.950
This is as far from idols as you can get,
but the crowd's loving it!

00:19:05.950 --> 00:19:09.830
And now, for our final act,
we'll perform a deadlift!

00:19:09.830 --> 00:19:11.950
Why am I the last to go?

00:19:11.950 --> 00:19:15.040
D-Dead...? What do they plan on doing?

00:19:15.040 --> 00:19:16.330
The deadlift.

00:19:19.120 --> 00:19:24.540
One of the Big Three of weight training,
along with the bench press and squats.

00:19:24.540 --> 00:19:26.700
That is the deadlift.

00:19:26.700 --> 00:19:28.790
Who in the world are you...?

00:19:28.790 --> 00:19:34.200
But it's said the deadlift has the highest
degree of difficulty of those three.

00:19:34.200 --> 00:19:39.160
"Squeeze shoulder blades, straighten back" "Gaze"
"Center of gravity in butt"
Bad posture puts your lower back
and spine at risk of injury.

00:19:39.160 --> 00:19:44.000
"Lift in one go
without arching your back"
She's attempting that dangerous
exercise on the big stage.

00:19:44.000 --> 00:19:46.080
No, just do it at the gym.

00:19:46.080 --> 00:19:49.000
This guy isn't an ordinary spectator...

00:19:49.000 --> 00:19:50.330
Who the hell is he?

00:19:54.660 --> 00:19:57.410
Take a breath and build stomach pressure.

00:19:58.660 --> 00:20:01.160
Use a mixed grip for the bar.

00:20:05.160 --> 00:20:06.790
Don't pull with your arms!

00:20:06.790 --> 00:20:08.330
Don't lift with your knees!

00:20:08.330 --> 00:20:12.040
Back, pelvis, hamstrings...

00:20:12.040 --> 00:20:14.660
Concentrate on your back!

00:20:20.160 --> 00:20:22.700
Deadlift, complete!

00:20:23.000 --> 00:20:26.000
"Public Idol Audition"

00:20:29.450 --> 00:20:32.580
Tachibana-<i>sensei</i>, nice dead.

00:20:32.580 --> 00:20:35.200
Thank you very much!

00:20:54.660 --> 00:20:58.910
Yeah, idols should be normal.

00:20:58.910 --> 00:21:02.910
"So Cool!
Public Idol Audition"
"Aspire to Be a Real Idol!"
Naturally, they didn't make the cut.

00:22:33.250 --> 00:22:34.870
Y'all shredded yet?

00:22:34.870 --> 00:22:38.250
"Lateral Raise"
Today, we'll do the lateral raise,
a shoulder exercise!

00:22:38.250 --> 00:22:41.700
"Lateral Raise"
Hold something of a reasonable
weight in each hand.

00:22:41.700 --> 00:22:45.580
Two-liter bottles filled with
water should be just right.

00:22:45.580 --> 00:22:48.410
First, spread your feet
shoulder-width apart,

00:22:48.410 --> 00:22:51.080
and bend forward slightly.

00:22:51.080 --> 00:22:55.040
Then slowly raise your arms horizontally.

00:22:55.040 --> 00:22:56.120
Make sure you avoid moving
your shoulder blades.

00:22:56.120 --> 00:22:58.910
"Avoid moving shoulder blades."
Make sure you avoid moving
your shoulder blades.

00:22:58.950 --> 00:23:02.540
You can do this while sitting, too,
so be sure to try it with us!

00:23:02.540 --> 00:23:04.250
We'll do 20 reps!

00:23:04.250 --> 00:23:06.250
Then let's get started!

00:23:07.500 --> 00:23:09.500
Mind your posture!

00:23:09.500 --> 00:23:11.120
Breathe in rhythm!

00:23:12.330 --> 00:23:15.120
Avoid going completely horizontal!

00:23:15.120 --> 00:23:18.450
Stop just before your arms are straight!

00:23:18.450 --> 00:23:22.200
And don't move your shoulder blades!

00:23:22.200 --> 00:23:25.330
Be aware of the muscles you're working on!

00:23:26.870 --> 00:23:28.330
Keep a good tempo!

00:23:29.160 --> 00:23:32.000
Well? You feeling it?

00:23:32.000 --> 00:23:33.500
Just a little more!

00:23:36.700 --> 00:23:41.120
--All done!
--Keep this up to get cool shoulders!

00:23:41.120 --> 00:23:42.700
And as always...

00:23:42.700 --> 00:23:44.910
Nice bulk!

00:23:44.910 --> 00:23:49.200
If you have time, continue at this
pace during the commercial break!
